"$$$/xmp/date_description=A date-time value which is represented using a subset of ISO RFC 8601 formatting, as described in YYYY MM = two-digit month (01=January) NOTE: The use of local times, using a time zone designator of +hh:mm or -hh:mm instead of Z, is recommended to promote human understanding. For example, if you know a file was saved at noon on October 23 a timestamp of 2004-10-23T12:00:00-06:00is understandable, while 2004-10-23T18:00:00Zis confusing."
"$$$/xmp/date_label=Date"
