"$$$/xmp/real_description=A numeric value of arbitrary precision. Consists of a decimal numeric string with an optional single decimal point and an optional leading \"+\" or \"-\" sign. It can optionally have the qualifier vQual:binRep, of type std size,endian,hexadecimal_value - endianis Lfor little-endian, B for big-endian."
"$$$/xmp/real_label=Real"
"$$$/xmp/seq_description=In the schema definitions, an ordered array is referred to as a seq. For example, dc:creator is defined as Sequence ProperName, meaning the order of the creators matters and each creator value is a proper name (defined elsewhere)."
