"$$$/xmp/xmp/Advisory_description=An unordered array specifying properties that were edited outside the authoring application. Each item should contain a single namespace and XPath separated by one ASCII space (U+0020)."
"$$$/xmp/xmp/Advisory_label=Advisory"
"$$$/xmp/xmp/BaseURL_description=The base URL for relative URLs in the document content. If this document contains Internet links, and those links are relative, they are relative to this base URL. This property provides a standard way for embedded relative URLs to be interpreted by tools. Web authoring tools should set the value based on their notion of where URLs will be interpreted."
"$$$/xmp/xmp/BaseURL_label=Base URL"
"$$$/xmp/xmp/CreateDate_description=The date and time the resource was originally created."
"$$$/xmp/xmp/CreateDate_label=Creation Date"
"$$$/xmp/xmp/CreatorTool_description=The name of the tool used to create the resource."
"$$$/xmp/xmp/CreatorTool_label=Creator Tool"
"$$$/xmp/xmp/Identifier_description=An unordered array of text strings that unambiguously identify the resource within a given context. An array item may be qualified with xmpidq:Scheme to denote the formal identification system to which that identifier conforms. NOTE: The dc:identifier property is not used because it lacks a defined scheme qualifier and has been defined in the XMP Specification as a simple (single-valued) property."
"$$$/xmp/xmp/Identifier_label=Identifier"
"$$$/xmp/xmp/Label_description=Collection member identifier."
"$$$/xmp/xmp/Label_label=Label"
"$$$/xmp/xmp/MetadataDate_description=The date and time that any metadata for this resource was last changed. It should be the same as or more recent than xmp:ModifyDate."
"$$$/xmp/xmp/MetadataDate_label=Metadata Date"
"$$$/xmp/xmp/ModifyDate_description=The date and time the resource was last modified. NOTE: The value of this property is not necessarily the same as the file’s system modification date because it is set before the file is saved."
"$$$/xmp/xmp/ModifyDate_label=Modification Date"
"$$$/xmp/xmp/Nickname_description=Informal name."
"$$$/xmp/xmp/Nickname_label=Nickname"
"$$$/xmp/xmp/Rating_description=The rating property allows the user to assign a fixed value (often “stars” to their assets. The range of values is from 0.0 to 5.0. The value can also be -1.0 to represent a “reject” rating. This means an asset should not be deleted, but not considered in further processing."
"$$$/xmp/xmp/Rating_label=Rating"
"$$$/xmp/xmp/Thumbnails_label=Thumbnails"
"$$$/xmp/xmp/custom/CreatorTool_label=Application"
"$$$/xmp/xmp/custom/logComment_label=Comments"
"$$$/xmp/xmpBJ/JobRef_description=References an external job management file for a job process in which the document is being used. Use of job names is under user control. Typical use would be to identify all documents that are part of a particular job or contract. There are multiple values because there can be more than one job using a particular document at any time, and it can also be useful to keep historical information about what jobs a document was part of previously."
"$$$/xmp/xmpBJ/JobRef_label=Job Ref"
"$$$/xmp/xmpBJ/job/id_description=Unique ID for the job. This field is a reference into some external job management system."
"$$$/xmp/xmpBJ/job/id_label=Id"
